    {
      "number": 6,
      "id": "PR_kwDOU86eg88AAAABG0j7sg",
      "title": "Require reliable reset and add Stream Sequence to subgroup streams",
      "url": "https://github.com/afrind/draft-frindell-moq-subscription-flow-control/pull/6",
      "state": "MERGED",
      "author": "afrind",
      "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "Addresses review feedback on PR #1 about correlating SUBGROUP_RESET with the reset stream. Group ID and Subgroup ID are not sufficient: a stream reset before its header arrives is unidentifiable, and a publisher can open more than one stream for the same subgroup.\r\n\r\n* Endpoints offering the extension MUST support RESET_STREAM_AT, and publishers MUST reset subgroup streams with a reliable_size covering the SUBGROUP_HEADER.\r\n* When the extension is negotiated, SUBGROUP_HEADER includes a per-subscription Stream Sequence. SUBGROUP_RESET identifies the stream by Stream Sequence instead of Group ID and Subgroup ID.\r\n* A Stream Sequence at or above the stream limit is FLOW_CONTROL_EXCEEDED; a detected duplicate is a PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-06T01:03:47Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-07T03:58:56Z",
      "baseRepository": "afrind/draft-frindell-moq-subscription-flow-control",
      "baseRefName": "main",
      "baseRefOid": "d4d1f1671f6f431aa7d4142b52f53b21821cc3fe",
      "headRepository": "afrind/draft-frindell-moq-subscription-flow-control",
      "headRefName": "require-reliable-reset",
      "headRefOid": "2d57d07fc955501ccc7239085c65c3c59e76a72c",
      "closedAt": "2026-10-07T03:58:53Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-07T03:58:53Z",
      "mergedBy": "afrind",
      "mergeCommit": {
        "oid": "f7399d25a7fe806823e44d0cc36942c5f5b17a09"
      },
      "comments": [],
      "reviews": [
        {
          "id": "PRR_kwDOU86eg88AAAABRArd8w",
          "commit": {
            "abbreviatedOid": "e85255d"
          },
          "author": "ianswett",
          "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
          "state": "APPROVED",
          "body": "I'm saddened by the complexity of this, but given Stream ID isn't exposed, I think it's a reasonable compromise.",
          "createdAt": "2026-10-07T01:24:29Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-10-07T01:24:29Z",
          "comments": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "id": "PR_kwDOU86eg88AAAABG0rf4A",
      "title": "Apply the Final Size check whenever the transport reports it",
      "url": "https://github.com/afrind/draft-frindell-moq-subscription-flow-control/pull/7",
      "state": "MERGED",
      "author": "afrind",
      "authorAssociation": "OWNER",
      "assignees": [],
      "labels": [],
      "body": "Addresses review feedback on PR #1 about WebTransport and the Final Size cross-check. WebTransport implementations do not necessarily expose a reset stream's final size; when the transport does report it, a mismatch with SUBGROUP_RESET is a PROTOCOL_VIOLATION.\r\n\r\n* Drop the FIN case, which never produces a SUBGROUP_RESET to check.\r\n* Trim the Security Considerations paragraph to describe the threat and point to Byte Accounting instead of restating the rule.",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-06T01:20:56Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-07T01:36:46Z",
      "baseRepository": "afrind/draft-frindell-moq-subscription-flow-control",
      "baseRefName": "main",
      "baseRefOid": "4c216ddc5b1fa87f63074c6b948bb8a4e88edffa",
      "headRepository": "afrind/draft-frindell-moq-subscription-flow-control",
      "headRefName": "webtransport-final-size",
      "headRefOid": "12c37524089ac6ac721b4605a95a98c7bdcd9ef0",
      "closedAt": "2026-10-07T01:36:43Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-07T01:36:42Z",
      "mergedBy": "ianswett",
      "mergeCommit": {
        "oid": "d4d1f1671f6f431aa7d4142b52f53b21821cc3fe"
      },
      "comments": [],
      "reviews": [
        {
          "id": "PRR_kwDOU86eg88AAAABQ_DobA",
          "commit": {
            "abbreviatedOid": "0193b2e"
          },
          "author": "ianswett",
          "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
          "state": "COMMENTED",
          "body": "Two questions/suggestions",
          "createdAt": "2026-10-06T21:35:08Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-10-06T21:37:24Z",
          "comments": [
